DATABASE_URL=postgres://miel:miel@localhost:5435/miel
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=miel
CLAUDE_BIN=claude
API_PORT=3001
WEB_PORT=3000
API_SECRET=change-me-to-a-random-string

# There is deliberately no CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN here. The long-lived Claude
# credential from `claude setup-token` is a runtime secret like every other AI
# credential: paste it once under Settings → AI & Triage → Credentials and it is
# stored encrypted in Postgres. Nothing reads it from the environment, so a value
# set here would be ignored. `claude-code` is the provider every task starts on,
# so a fresh install triages once that token is pasted — until then triage and
# replies fail with a clear "not configured" message.

# In-app Google OAuth ("Connect with Google"). Create a "Web application" OAuth
# client in Google Cloud Console and register the redirect URI(s) below.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/auth/google/callback

# AES-256-GCM key (base64, 32 bytes) for encrypting secrets at rest — Google
# refresh tokens and LLM provider API keys. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Optional in dev (falls back to plaintext with a warning); REQUIRED in prod.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# There is deliberately no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here (#104), nor one for Google or
# OpenAI (#105), nor any WORP_* key (#107). A hosted provider's key is a runtime
# credential: paste it once under Settings → AI & Triage → Credentials and it is
# stored encrypted in Postgres, because the provider picker that uses it is
# itself a runtime setting. See docs/adr/0001-provider-credentials-in-postgres.md.

# Local dev only: Vite reads these at build time and bakes them into the SPA bundle.
# In prod they MUST be passed as Docker build args to the @miel/web image, NOT as
# runtime env (changing them at runtime has no effect).
VITE_API_BASE=/api
VITE_API_SECRET=change-me-to-a-random-string

# worp ingest integration: no env vars. The relay's base URL, its API key and
# any headers needed to reach it through a proxy are runtime settings, entered
# under Settings → Integrations → worp and stored in Postgres (the key and the
# headers encrypted, like a provider key). Until they are set the route answers
# worp_not_configured rather than 500. If you are upgrading from a build that
# read WORP_* from here, enter the same values once in Settings and delete them
# from this file — nothing is imported from the environment.

# --- prod only (Dokploy) ---
# The public hostname the deployment is reached through — the single host the
# landing container (/), the app (/app) and the same-origin API proxy (/api) all
# share. Read by the deploy topology (packages/landing-page/src/deploy/
# topology.ts) and the deployment docs; it defaults to the host DEPLOY.md walks
# through, so the reference deployment needs nothing set here. Hosting miel
# somewhere else means setting this, not editing source.
# SITE_HOST=miel.example.org

# Comma-separated allowlist of allowed CORS origins for the API. Also the base
# the OAuth callback sends the browser back to; keep it a bare scheme://host —
# the app's /app path prefix is appended in code. Example:
# WEB_ORIGIN=https://miel.gousse.cool
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# Prod redirect URI (register this in the Google OAuth client alongside the
# localhost one). The API is reverse-proxied under /api by Traefik:
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://miel.gousse.cool/api/auth/google/callback
